string("// EffectsApp is the project's app payload struct. It holds configuration data\n// and dependency handlers for logging, time, and console output. Reads like\n// `EffectsApp.logger` reach the active app value.\n//\n// Dependency fields (logger, clock, console) are interface-typed because\n// that is the shape this project wants. App access treats them the same\n// as data fields: code reads the fields it needs as `EffectsApp.field`.\n//\n// `load` dispatches by deployment name; each builder returns a fully-constructed\n// EffectsApp with both data fields and dependency handlers.\nimport {\n    dev\n    effects.{Clock, Console, Logger}\n    prod\n    test as test_env\n}\n\n// Boot passes a root Context to the selected application constructor.\npub struct EffectsApp {\n    context: Context\n\n    deployment: String = \"dev\"\n    port: Int = 3000\n    database_url: String = \"postgres://localhost/myapp_dev\"\n    max_connections: Int = 5\n    logger: Logger\n    clock: Clock\n    console: Console\n}\n\npub fn load(deployment: String, context: Context): EffectsApp {\n    case deployment {\n        \"prod\" -> prod.build(context)\n        \"test\" -> test_env.build(context)\n        _ -> dev.build(context)\n    }\n}\n")
